      "content": "1.                                             HIGH STREET 839                                            (South Side)                                                No 275                                                (Boxwell House) SP 98()I NE 3/35              SP 9808 SE 4/35              29.7.50.             II 2.  Late C17 or early C18 of symmetrical design with steep central pediment. Cement rendered brickwork, Welsh slated roof, hipped., formerly tiled, 2 storeys, quoins; central projecting bay with doorway having Roman Ionic attached columns; entablature with pulvinated frieze, modillioned pediment. 1:2:1 sashes with glazing bars in architrave surrounds, bracketed sills.  Modillions to roof cornice and pediment.  Back elevation much altered. Listing NGR: SP9879408002"
    }
